option.FOXY_EXPOSURE.comment=Global exposure before final tonemapping.
option.FOXY_POST_EXPOSURE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts final brightness after automatic exposure.
option.FOXY_AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=Automatically adjusts exposure to scene brightness.
option.FOXY_AUTO_EXPOSURE_DARK_LIMIT.comment=Maximum auto-exposure gain in dark scenes. Lower keeps caves genuinely dark.
option.FOXY_AUTO_EXPOSURE_BRIGHT_LIMIT.comment=Maximum auto-exposure darkening in bright scenes. Lower keeps the sky from being dragged down by bright ground such as sand or snow.
option.FOXY_BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Bloom strength. 0 turns it off.
option.FOXY_MOTION_BLUR.comment=Camera motion blur amount. Higher values allow stronger camera blur.
option.FOXY_CLOUDS.comment=Enables procedural volumetric clouds.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=Higher quality improves cloud detail at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_STEPS.comment=Higher values reduce cloud banding at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_LIGHT_STEPS.comment=Higher values improve cloud lighting and self-shadowing at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_LIGHT_DITHER.comment=Depth of the light-march jitter. Too low leaves hard light/dark bands in the clouds; too high replaces them with visible per-pixel noise. Look at a sunlit cloud side and lower it until the grain settles.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_LIGHT_DITHER_ENABLED.comment=Fixes most of the light/dark banding at the cloud base, but noticeably increases noise.
value.FOXY_CLOUD_LIGHT_DITHER_ENABLED.0=Off
value.FOXY_CLOUD_LIGHT_DITHER_ENABLED.1=On
option.FOXY_CLOUD_RANGE.comment=Controls how far volumetric clouds are rendered.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_WORLD_SCALE.comment=Adjusts the overall scale of the cloudscape.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_HEIGHT.comment=World Y height of the main volumetric cloud base.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=Vertical thickness of the main volumetric cloud layer.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=How much of the sky is covered by procedural cloud fields.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_RAIN_COVERAGE.comment=The cloud coverage the sky settles at while it rains, blended in from Cloud Coverage by rain strength (85% of the way at full rain). Rain used to pile straight onto the clear-sky coverage and seal the sky into one solid overcast, so rain gets its own target instead: keeping it near the clear value lets a rainy sky look heavy without swallowing the horizon. Raise it for a more oppressive downpour, lower it for thinner rain cloud.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_DENSITY.comment=Controls cloud opacity.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_BOTTOM_EROSION_SIZE.comment=Controls the horizontal size of cloud-bottom erosion regions. Higher values produce broader individual features.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_BOTTOM_RELIEF.comment=Adjusts the amount of shape variation along cloud bottoms.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_SPEED.comment=Controls cloud movement speed.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly procedural clouds attenuate direct sunlight on terrain. §e[*]§r LOD terrain (Voxy / Distant Horizons) is not supported yet: the shadow only reaches terrain inside the vanilla render distance.\nOnly direct sunlight is affected, never ambient light.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_SHAPE_BASE_SCALE.comment=Adjusts the size of broad cloud formations.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_SHAPE_DETAIL_SCALE.comment=Adjusts the scale of fine cloud-edge detail.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_CLOUD_SIZE.comment=Adjusts overall cloud size.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_HORIZONTAL_COVERAGE_BIAS.comment=Adjusts horizontal cloud coverage.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_VERTICAL_COVERAGE_BIAS.comment=Adjusts how clouds fill their vertical layer.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_CUMULUS_BIAS.comment=Biases cloud type toward cumulus-style vertical development.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_EROSION_SCALE.comment=Size of the bumps under the clouds. Higher values make each feature broader.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_BOTTOM_DENSITY_POWER.comment=Adjusts density near the bottom of clouds.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_HEIGHT_GRADIENT_SCALE.comment=Vertical scale applied to the height gradient.
option.FOXY_CLOUD_HEIGHT_GRADIENT_CONTRAST.comment=Contrast applied to the height gradient.
option.FOXY_RAY_MODE.comment=§7AO§r: vanilla ambient occlusion, cheapest and softest.\n§2RSM§r: reflective shadow map bounce. It can only give direct light a colored reflection; it adds nothing indoors, but it improves the quality of sunlight. Low performance cost, but noisy.\n§aSSPT§r: screen-space ray tracing, cheaper than global tracing, but the light vanishes once it leaves the screen.\n§eIRC§r: same cost as SSPT and the light survives off-screen, but the precision is poor.\n§6IRC+SSPT§r: SSPT's precision filling in IRC's off-screen light, roughly equivalent to VRTGI, better on AMD cards - pick this if VRTGI fails to load.\n§cVRTGI§r: standard global voxel ray tracing, the most detail and lighting stability with the fewest rendering problems.\n§4VRTGI+SSPT§r: SSPT fills in lighting detail and takes part in the fallback beyond the voxel range; the most expensive and not finished, so it shows many light/dark seams.
option.FOXY_SSPT_SPP.comment=Higher values reduce SSPT noise at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_SSPT_TRACE_STEPS.comment=Higher values improve SSPT reach and stability at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_SSPT_MAX_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum distance for SSPT indirect lighting.
option.FOXY_SSPT_HISTORY_FRAMES.comment=Higher values reduce stable-scene noise but respond more slowly to changes.
option.FOXY_SSPT_DENOISE_QUALITY.comment=Higher quality produces cleaner indirect lighting at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_SSPT_DENOISE_STRENGTH.comment=Controls how strongly indirect-light noise is smoothed.
option.FOXY_SSPT_BOUNCE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts SSPT indirect-light brightness.
option.FOXY_RSM_INTENSITY.comment=Overall brightness of the RSM bounce.
option.FOXY_RSM_RADIUS.comment=Gather radius in light space, in blocks. Larger pulls in more lit surfaces and softens the result at no extra cost.
option.FOXY_RSM_SAMPLES.comment=Number of disk samples. Higher is smoother; this is the only performance knob for the RSM mode.
option.FOXY_RSM_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum distance to a secondary light source, in blocks. Lit surfaces beyond it do not contribute.
option.FOXY_SSPT_MINIMUM_LIGHT.comment=Keeps fully unlit surfaces from becoming completely black.
option.FOXY_SSPT_MINIMUM_LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts the brightness of the minimum-light safeguard.
option.FOXY_ENTITY_BASE_LIGHT.comment=Adds a base ambient floor to entities and other non-terrain surfaces.
option.FOXY_SSPT_DENOISER.comment=Smooths SSPT and VRTGI noise. Disable only if you prefer the raw result.
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Adjusts the angle of the sun and moon path.
option.FOXY_SUN_INTENSITY.comment=Adjusts sunlight brightness.
option.FOXY_MOON_INTENSITY.comment=Adjusts moonlight brightness.
option.FOXY_AMBIENT_INTENSITY.comment=Adjusts the brightness of ambient sky lighting.
option.FOXY_SSPT_ENVIRONMENT_BOUNCE.comment=Allows sky and local light to contribute to SSPT indirect lighting.
option.FOXY_SSPT_EMISSIVE_FEEDBACK.comment=Lets emissive materials contribute to SSPT indirect lighting.
option.FOXY_SSPT_EMISSIVE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts indirect lighting from emissive materials.
option.FOXY_VXGI_TRUE_SECONDARY_BOUNCE.comment=Adds a second VRTGI light bounce. This can noticeably increase performance cost.
option.FOXY_VRTGI_REALISTIC_MODE.comment=Uses a brighter, more natural VRTGI lighting balance.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_INTENSITY.comment=Adjusts overall VRTGI indirect-light brightness.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_SPP.comment=Higher values reduce VRTGI noise at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_VRTGI_RESOLUTION.comment=Higher values improve detail and stability but use more GPU performance and memory.
option.FOXY_VRTGI_TEMPORAL_INTERLEAVE.comment=Reduces VRTGI tracing cost with slightly slower convergence.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_DISTANCE_CHUNKS.comment=Controls VRTGI range. Higher values use more GPU memory and performance.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_MAX_STEPS.comment=Higher values improve VRTGI coverage at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_IRRADIANCE_CACHE.comment=Improves VRTGI stability when moving through the world.
option.FOXY_IRRADIANCE_CACHE_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts indirect lighting supplied by the irradiance cache.
option.FOXY_IRRADIANCE_CACHE_SKY_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts cached sky-light contribution.
option.FOXY_IRRADIANCE_CACHE_BLOCK_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts cached local-light contribution.
option.FOXY_IRRADIANCE_CACHE_HISTORY_FRAMES.comment=Higher values are steadier; lower values react faster to lighting changes.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_SUN_DIFFUSE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts sunlit diffuse contribution in VRTGI.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_EMITTER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts VRTGI contribution from emissive blocks and local lights.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_GI_SKY_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts VRTGI contribution from the sky.
option.FOXY_PBR.comment=Enables PBR materials from compatible resource packs.
option.FOXY_PBR_SPECULAR_MAPS.comment=Uses resource-pack specular maps for reflections, metals and emissive materials.
option.FOXY_PBR_NORMAL_MAPS.comment=Uses resource-pack normal maps for detailed surface lighting.
option.FOXY_PBR_TEXTURE_FORMAT.comment=Selects how specular and normal maps are decoded.
option.FOXY_PBR_EMISSION_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Adjusts the visible brightness of emissive resource-pack textures.
option.FOXY_PBR_SPECULAR_STRENGTH.comment=Adjusts sun and moon highlights on PBR materials.
option.FOXY_PBR_FALLBACK_F0.comment=Adjusts reflections when no specular map is available.
option.FOXY_PBR_LIGHT_ANGULAR_RADIUS.comment=Adjusts the softness of sharp PBR highlights.
option.FOXY_PBR_SPECULAR_CLAMP.comment=Limits overly bright PBR highlights.
option.FOXY_PBR_METAL_DIFFUSE.comment=Adjusts diffuse lighting on metals without specular maps.
option.FOXY_PBR_SSS.comment=Allows sunlight and moonlight to pass through thin foliage.
option.FOXY_PBR_SSS_INTENSITY.comment=Adjusts light transmission through leaves and grass.
option.FOXY_PBR_SSS_ALPHA_NEIGHBORS.comment=Improves foliage-edge translucency at a small performance cost.
option.FOXY_PBR_SSS_SHEEN.comment=Adds soft edge highlights to grass and other thin plants.
option.FOXY_SKY_SCATTER_EXPOSURE.comment=Overall brightness of the sky scattering. Lower values keep the sky from washing out.
option.FOXY_SKY_HORIZON_WHITE.comment=White aerosol haze just above the horizon. Lower values reveal more blue, gold, and red.
option.FOXY_SKY_BLUE_DEPTH.comment=Deepens and preserves the upper-sky blue without changing global exposure.
option.FOXY_SKY_SUNSET_WARMTH.comment=Warmth of the sky at sunset. Higher values make it redder and dim the sun.
option.FOXY_SKY_BELOW_HORIZON_LIFT.comment=How bright the sky stays just below the horizon line. Lower it to let the ground under the horizon read darker and closer to haze; at 0 the area below the horizon uses the true ground value.
option.FOXY_SKY_BELOW_HORIZON_RANGE.comment=How far below the horizon the brightness carries before settling to the dark value. Larger spreads the falloff over more of the lower screen; too small brings back a flat band.
option.FOXY_SKY_VANILLA_CELESTIALS.comment=Uses Minecraft's sun and moon textures while keeping atmospheric tint, exposure, and bloom.
option.FOXY_SKY_VANILLA_MOON.comment=Shows Minecraft's eight moon phases when vanilla celestial textures are disabled.
option.FOXY_NASA_GALAXY.comment=Shows a detailed Milky Way panorama in the night sky.
option.FOXY_NASA_GALAXY_INTENSITY.comment=Adjusts the brightness of the Milky Way panorama.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_SKY.comment=When off, the End keeps the original sky; when on, the black hole is used as the End sky background (End only).
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_SUN.comment=Shows a black hole where the Overworld sun is. The framing and brightness come from the sun black hole options below.
value.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_SUN.0=Off
value.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_SUN.1=On
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_GALAXY_EXPOSURE.comment=Brightness of the galaxy behind the black hole.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_REFLECTION_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the black hole and its disk in reflections off water, glass and ice. §e[*]§r Only visible once the sun or moon black hole is on.\nDoes not change how bright the black hole looks in the sky.\nHigher values bring the water back toward the strength the old sun glitter had.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_SPIN.comment=Black hole spin. Higher values shift the central shadow to one side and pull the inner edge of the disk closer in.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_CAM_DIST.comment=Observer distance from the black hole in radii. Smaller looks bigger.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_CAM_PITCH.comment=Observer elevation above the disk plane (degrees); near 0 is edge-on, larger looks down onto the disk.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_CAM_YAW.comment=Observer angle around the spin axis; sets the disk bright side and pattern orientation.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_TILT.comment=Tilt of the accretion disk. 0 lies flat; higher values stand it up at an angle.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_FOLLOW.comment=Anchors the black hole in the world, so walking closer or further away gives real parallax. Off keeps it locked to the camera.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_FOLLOW_SCALE.comment=Blocks per black hole radius, used while Follow Player Position is on. Lower values swing the viewpoint faster as you fly.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_ORBIT.comment=Flies the camera around the black hole on an elliptical path, between its closest and furthest point.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_ORBIT_SPEED.comment=Orbital angular speed (radians/second); sets how fast the plunge happens. 0 parks the camera at the aphelion.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_ORBIT_NEAR.comment=Closest point of the orbit. At 0 the camera falls all the way in and the sky it passes turns black.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_ORBIT_FAR.comment=Furthest point of the orbit.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_TETRAD_CAMERA.comment=Frames the view the way a real observer would. Approaching the black hole shifts the whole image blue and brighter.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_AUTO_ROTATE.comment=Auto-rotation speed of the disk pattern and background galaxy. 0 is static.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DISK_OPACITY.comment=How dense the accretion disk is. Higher values make it more opaque and hide more of what is behind it.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DOPPLER.comment=Brightness difference between the two sides of the disk. Higher values brighten the side rotating toward you and darken the other; 0 makes them equal.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DOPPLER_EXP.comment=How steep that brightness difference is. Higher values make the contrast more extreme.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DISK_EMIT.comment=Surface brightness of the accretion disk.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DISK_ABSORB.comment=How strongly the disk absorbs light. Together with the opacity above, it sets how solid the disk looks.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DISK_TEMP.comment=Colour temperature of the disk. Lower is amber gold, higher is blue-white. It also changes the colour of the End's direct light.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_TEMP_CONTRAST.comment=Color temperature spread across the disk. 0 is uniform; higher gives a bluer core and redder rim.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DISK_OUTER.comment=Outer radius of the accretion disk. Higher values make the disk wider. §7§oPerformance: §eMedium
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_DISK_FLARE.comment=Thickness of the disk. Higher values make it look like a three-dimensional cloud; lower keeps it thin.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_TURB.comment=When off, the disk turbulence becomes a flat color field.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_TURB_SCALE.comment=Overall scale of the disk turbulence. Higher packs in finer filaments; too high only blurs.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_FINE_STEP.comment=Extra precision while tracing the disk. Off is faster but loses detail on thin disks. §7§oPerformance: §6High
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_STEPS.comment=Maximum ray steps. Higher completes the photon ring at a higher cost.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_ESCAPE.comment=Radius of the black hole's influence. Smaller is cheaper.
option.FOXY_BLACKHOLE_EROSION.comment=Adds eroded fine detail to the disk surface.
option.FOXY_FOG_DENSITY.comment=Distance-based atmospheric fog density.
option.FOXY_FOG_START.comment=Higher values keep the near and mid view clearer before fog accelerates near the view edge.
option.FOXY_WORLD_FOG_STRENGTH.comment=Controls simple height fog when volumetric lighting is disabled.
option.FOXY_WORLD_FOG_HEIGHT.comment=Sets the base height of simple fog and distant cloud haze.
option.FOXY_WORLD_FOG_FALLOFF.comment=Controls how quickly simple fog fades with height.
option.FOXY_AIR_AEROSOL_ENABLED.comment=Enables dense atmospheric haze near the ground.
option.FOXY_AIR_AEROSOL_DENSITY.comment=Controls the density of low-altitude haze.
option.FOXY_AIR_AEROSOL_FADE_START.comment=Height where low-altitude haze begins to fade.
option.FOXY_AIR_AEROSOL_FADE_END.comment=Height where low-altitude haze fully disappears.
option.FOXY_AIR_MOLECULAR_ENABLED.comment=Enables lighter atmospheric haze at higher altitudes.
option.FOXY_AIR_MOLECULAR_DENSITY.comment=Controls the density of high-altitude haze.
option.FOXY_AIR_MOLECULAR_FADE_START.comment=Height where high-altitude haze begins to fade.
option.FOXY_AIR_MOLECULAR_FADE_END.comment=Height where high-altitude haze fully disappears.
option.FOXY_AIR_DENSITY_NOON.comment=Fog density multiplier while the sun is high.
option.FOXY_AIR_DENSITY_DAYLIGHT.comment=Fog density multiplier between sunrise and noon.
option.FOXY_AIR_DENSITY_TWILIGHT.comment=Fog density multiplier around sunrise and sunset.
option.FOXY_AIR_DENSITY_NIGHT.comment=Fog density multiplier at night. Moonlight and skylight still light the fog.
option.FOXY_AIR_TEMPERATURE_TWILIGHT.comment=Dawn and dusk scattering tint. 6500 K is neutral; lower is warmer.
option.FOXY_AIR_TEMPERATURE_NOON.comment=Noon scattering tint. 6500 K is neutral; lower is warmer.
option.FOXY_VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT.comment=Enables light shafts and volumetric fog.
option.FOXY_VL_CLUMPY_FOG.comment=Enables low-altitude cloud-like fog banks that thicken at sunrise and sunset.
option.FOXY_VL_QUALITY.comment=Higher quality reduces artifacts at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_VL_RESOLUTION.comment=Higher values improve volumetric detail at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_VL_STRENGTH.comment=Scattered sun/moon light contribution before final tonemapping.
option.FOXY_VL_DISTANCE.comment=Controls the visible range of directional light shafts.
option.FOXY_VL_SHADOWING.comment=Terrain and cloud occlusion of direct volumetric light. 1.0 gives the clearest shafts.
option.FOXY_VL_SHADOW_DARKEN.comment=Darkens transitions between shafts without brightening the entire fog layer. Higher values produce harder edges.
option.FOXY_VL_CLUMPINESS.comment=Controls the amount of variation in volumetric fog.
option.FOXY_WATER_REFLECTION.comment=Sky reflection and screen-space reflected silhouettes on water.
option.FOXY_WATER_REFLECTION_STRETCH.comment=Adjusts the reach of water reflections.
option.FOXY_WATER_SUN_GLINT.comment=Adjusts sunlight glitter on water.
option.FOXY_WATER_SPECTRUM_WAVES.comment=Enables animated multi-scale water waves.
option.FOXY_DH_LOD_TEXTURES.comment=Replaces the averaged block colour of Distant Horizons LOD terrain with the real block atlas texture. Requires an Iris build that exposes the DH LOD texture API (dh_sampleTexture); on older Iris builds this option fails to compile, so leave it off until Iris is updated.
option.FOXY_WATER_WAVE_STRENGTH.comment=Procedural water wave normal and surface displacement strength.
option.FOXY_WATER_CAUSTICS.comment=Enables moving light patterns beneath water.
option.FOXY_WATER_CAUSTICS_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of the underwater caustics. 0 turns them off.
option.FOXY_WATER_FOG.comment=Absorption and scattering strength through water.
option.FOXY_WATER_DENSITY.comment=Overall thickness of the water, affecting absorption, scattering and underwater fog together.
option.FOXY_WATER_SCATTER_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Underwater and water-volume scattering brightness, independent of reflections, caustics, and absorption.
option.FOXY_SHADOW_QUALITY.comment=Higher quality produces smoother, more stable shadows at a higher performance cost.
option.FOXY_SHADOW_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly occlusion darkens direct sunlight.
option.FOXY_VOXEL_DDA_HARD_SHADOW.comment=Hard-edged voxel shadows with no softening or light leaking. Relatively expensive.
option.FOXY_SHADOW_DISTANCE.comment=Furthest shadow distance in blocks. With Distant Horizons it must exceed the vanilla render distance to cover the LODs.
option.FOXY_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.comment=Higher values sharpen shadows but use more GPU memory and performance.
value.FOXY_SHADOW_QUALITY.0=Fast
value.FOXY_VOXEL_DDA_HARD_SHADOW.0=Off
value.FOXY_VOXEL_DDA_HARD_SHADOW.1=On
value.FOXY_SHADOW_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.FOXY_SHADOW_QUALITY.2=High
value.FOXY_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.1024=1024 × 1024
value.FOXY_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.1536=1536 × 1536
value.FOXY_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.2048=2048 × 2048
value.FOXY_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.3072=3072 × 3072
value.FOXY_SHADOW_RESOLUTION.4096=4096 × 4096
option.FOXY_TAA_ENABLED=Temporal Anti-Aliasing
option.FOXY_TAA_ENABLED.comment=Reduces jagged edges and shimmering, but may introduce mild ghosting in motion.
value.FOXY_TAA_ENABLED.0=Off
value.FOXY_TAA_ENABLED.1=On
option.FOXY_TAAU=Temporal Upscaling
option.FOXY_TAAU.comment=Improves performance by rendering below native resolution. Requires TAA and may reduce clarity.
value.FOXY_TAAU.0=Off
value.FOXY_TAAU.1=On
option.FOXY_TAAU_RENDER_SCALE=TAAU Render Scale
option.FOXY_TAAU_RENDER_SCALE.comment=Lower values improve performance but reduce image clarity.
option.FOXY_TAA_JITTER=TAA Jitter Amplitude
option.FOXY_TAA_JITTER.comment=TAA subpixel jitter amount. Higher smooths edges further but can add motion ghosting.
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX=Parallax (POM)
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_DEPTH=Parallax Depth
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_DEPTH.comment=Depth of the parallax relief. Higher values make the surface look deeper.
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_STEPS=Parallax Steps
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_STEPS.comment=Trace steps for parallax. Higher values keep the relief accurate at glancing angles. §7§oPerformance: §eMedium
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_DISTANCE=Parallax Distance
option.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_DISTANCE.comment=Furthest distance in blocks where parallax is applied. Beyond it the surface stays flat.
option.FOXY_LEAF_TRANSMISSION=Leaf / Grass Transmission
option.FOXY_LEAF_TRANSMISSION.comment=Master switch for light passing through thin vegetation, and for the soft skylight on the shaded side of leaves. Turning it off keeps the strength settings below but stops them taking effect.
value.FOXY_LEAF_TRANSMISSION.0=Off
value.FOXY_LEAF_TRANSMISSION.1=On
screen.FOXY_PBR_MATERIAL_OPTIONS=Material Parameters
screen.FOXY_PBR_TRANSMISSION_OPTIONS=Transmission
screen.FOXY_PBR_PARALLAX_OPTIONS=Parallax
option.FOXY_MATERIAL_REFLECTIONS=Material Reflections
option.FOXY_MATERIAL_REFLECTION_HIGH_QUALITY=High Quality Material Reflections
option.FOXY_MATERIAL_REFLECTION_GLOBAL=Global Material Reflections
option.FOXY_MATERIAL_REFLECTION_OFFSCREEN=Offscreen Reflection Material Supplement
option.FOXY_MATERIAL_REFLECTION_STEPS=Reflection Trace Steps
option.FOXY_MATERIAL_REFLECTION_STEPS.comment=Trace steps for screen-space reflections. Higher values reach further. §7§oPerformance: §eMedium
