option.FOXY_SEASONS=Season cycle
value.FOXY_SEASONS.0=Off
value.FOXY_SEASONS.1=On
option.FOXY_SEASONS.comment=Cycles the four seasons by world day. Autumn rotates the hue of green so leaves go from green to yellow and orange; winter drives leaves, grass and plants toward snow white. Summer and winter also change how much direct sunlight there is. The sun's path angle is not part of this and stays the pack's own Sun Path Rotation setting on the Sky page. Six days per season by default, so 24 days make one round.
option.FOXY_SEASON_DAYS=Days per season
option.FOXY_SEASON_DAYS.comment=How long each season lasts; the four seasons together make one cycle.
option.FOXY_SEASON_TRANSITION=Season changeover (days)
option.FOXY_SEASON_TRANSITION.comment=The last few days of each season fade into the next one. The rest of the season holds its state instead of drifting the whole time.
option.FOXY_SEASON_STRENGTH=Season strength
option.FOXY_SEASON_STRENGTH.comment=Scales the whole year, colour and direct sunlight alike; 0 keeps the cycle running but changes nothing.
option.FOXY_SEASON_AUTUMN_HUE=Autumn hue
option.FOXY_SEASON_AUTUMN_HUE.comment=The hue autumn drives green leaves to: 0.07 toward orange, 0.09 yellow-orange, 0.13 toward yellow, 0.17 golden.
option.FOXY_SEASON_AUTUMN_SATURATION=Autumn saturation
option.FOXY_SEASON_AUTUMN_SATURATION.comment=How vivid the autumn colours come out; higher is richer.
option.FOXY_SEASON_AUTUMN_BRIGHTNESS=Autumn brightness
option.FOXY_SEASON_AUTUMN_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Autumn's foliage brightness; a small lift makes the yellows glow more.
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_WHITENESS=Winter snow whiteness
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_WHITENESS.comment=How far winter drives leaves, grass and plants toward snow white. Autumn is not affected; 0 keeps the pack's own colours, 1 buries the vegetation in snow.
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_DETAIL=Winter snow detail
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_DETAIL.comment=How much of the texture's own brightness survives under the snow. Higher keeps leaf shape and shading readable; lower flattens the vegetation into one sheet of white.
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_R=Winter snow red
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_R.comment=Red of the winter snow colour. The default trio 0.90 / 0.94 / 1.00 is a cool white; raise all three for a brighter snow.
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_G=Winter snow green
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_G.comment=Green of the winter snow colour; with red and blue it sets what "snow white" means on your resource pack.
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_B=Winter snow blue
option.FOXY_SEASON_WINTER_B.comment=Blue of the winter snow colour. Slightly above red and green gives snow its cold tint; all three equal gives a neutral white.
option.FOXY_SEASON_SUN_ILLUMINANCE_SUMMER=Summer direct sunlight
option.FOXY_SEASON_SUN_ILLUMINANCE_SUMMER.comment=Summer's direct sunlight as a multiple of the pack's own - terrain, clouds and water reflections all follow it.
option.FOXY_SEASON_SUN_ILLUMINANCE_WINTER=Winter direct sunlight
option.FOXY_SEASON_SUN_ILLUMINANCE_WINTER.comment=Winter's direct sunlight multiple.

profile.FOXY_LIGHTWEIGHT=§eLightweight
profile.FOXY_STANDARD=§aStandard
profile.FOXY_HIGH_STANDARD=§bHigh Standard
profile.FOXY_SCREEN_TRACE=§3Screen-Space Ray Tracing
profile.FOXY_GLOBAL_TRACE=§dStandard Global Ray Tracing
profile.FOXY_GLOBAL_TRACE_STYLE=§5Special-Style Global Ray Tracing
profile.FOXY_EXTREME_CINEMA=§6PPT
profile.comment=§eLightweight§r: low performance cost and a clean image. Suited to a casual playthrough.\n§aStandard§r: stays smooth while still covering most of the shaders' content and atmosphere.\n§bHigh Standard§r: a stronger Standard with more reflection support.\n§3Screen-Space Ray Tracing§r: a global-illumination look; indirect light disappears once it leaves the screen. Fairly high performance cost.\n§dStandard Global Ray Tracing§r: global ray tracing with full reflective material support. For shader enthusiasts. High performance cost.\n§5Special-Style Global Ray Tracing§r: builds on Standard Global Ray Tracing but aims for the look of hardware ray tracing / Bedrock ray tracing, with fuller lighting that does not read as a Java shader.\n§6PPT§r: built specifically to §cblow§6 up§c your§6 computer§r.
